This directory contains many subdirectories

lib/ after compilation contains all plumed files which should be in the path
maketools/ contains some tool necessary for compilation

Then these directories are built and linked using special rules:
config/  contains some files generated based on system configuration
main/    contains the main() program for plumed executable
wrapper/ contains the wrappers for MD codes

All the other directories are "modules". Modules are of three type:
* always compiled (necessary for plumed to properly link)
* default on, can be disabled with ./configure --enable-modules=-modulename
* default off, can be enabled with ./configure --enable-modules=+modulename

Configure stores module overrides in the PLUMED_MODULE_ENABLED and PLUMED_MODULE_DISABLED variables in
../Makefile.conf. Unlisted modules follow their current module.yml default,
including modules added after configuration. Required dependencies are enabled
during configuration. Legacy modulename.on and modulename.off files are ignored.

The type and native dependencies are declared in module.yml (see core/module.yml).
See ../conda/module-options.md for the shared declaration format.
